<Base title="Gift Re Pricing Lab" description="WGAN-GP + Extreme Value Theory catastrophe reinsurance pricing prototype for Indian perils. Runs in the browser on public data." wide={true}>
  <iframe class="app-frame" src="/apps/pricing-lab/" title="Gift Re Pricing Lab" loading="eager"></iframe>
  <div class="wrap" style="padding-block:20px"><p class="notice">Research prototype built for a doctoral dissertation on AI-native reinsurance. Public economic-loss data, illustrative assumptions, not a quotation. <a href="/blog/pricing-catastrophes-with-wgan-and-evt/">Method and data are described here</a>. The W-GAN models were trained with AI assistance (Claude) and are documented in that blog post; open the app in its own tab at <a href="/apps/pricing-lab/">/apps/pricing-lab/</a>.</p><p class="notice" style="margin-top:10px"><b>Dissertation result (October 2026):</b> against a lognormal benchmark, the EVT-calibrated W-GAN is more accurate in the tail (the lognormal overstates 1-in-100 flood and cyclone losses by 70–90% and prices layers 15–20% higher) and captures the correlation of drought across regions, but its premium is not more stable under resampling. The full tables are in the <a href="/blog/pricing-catastrophes-with-wgan-and-evt/#results-reported-in-the-dissertation-october-2026">method post</a>.</p></div>
</Base>
